+# Registering the request-id middleware
+
+Register `RequestIdMiddleware` as global middleware in the root module, exactly
+like any other cross-cutting `NestMiddleware`:
+
+```ts
+import { MiddlewareConsumer, Module, NestModule } from '@nestjs/common';
+import { RequestIdMiddleware } from '@nestjs/core';
+
+@Module({ /* ... */ })
+export class AppModule implements NestModule {
+  configure(consumer: MiddlewareConsumer) {
+    consumer.apply(RequestIdMiddleware).forRoutes('*');
+  }
+}
+```
+
+This is the only wiring required, and it is identical whether the application is
+bootstrapped with `NestExpressApplication` or `NestFastifyApplication` — both
+route global middleware through the same `AbstractHttpAdapter#use` call.
+
+Once registered, every response — including 404s and responses produced by
+exception filters — carries the `x-request-id` header, reusing the caller's own
+header value when one was sent, or a freshly generated id otherwise.
+
+To read the same id from inside a request (a service, guard, interceptor, or a
+log line), call `getRequestId()` anywhere during that request; it returns
+exactly the value written onto the response header, with no need to inject the
+raw request object or re-parse the header:
+
+```ts
+import { Injectable, Logger } from '@nestjs/common';
+import { getRequestId } from '@nestjs/core';
+
+@Injectable()
+export class OrdersService {
+  private readonly logger = new Logger(OrdersService.name);
+
+  placeOrder() {
+    this.logger.log(`placing order [requestId=${getRequestId()}]`);
+  }
+}
+```
